For $R_{1}$; 2x + y = 10 and x, y $\in$ N possible values for x and y are :

x = 1, y = 8    i.e.   (1, 8);

x = 2, y = 6    i.e    (2, 6);

x = 3, y = 4    i.e    (3, 4);

x = 4, y = 2    i.e    (4, 2)

$\therefore\,\,\, R_{1}$ = { (1, 8), (2, 6), (3, 4), (4, 2) }

$\therefore\,\,\,$ Range of $R_{1}$ is {2, 4, 6, 8}

$R_{1}$ is not symmetric.

$R_{1}$ is not transitive also as

(3, 4), (4, 2) $\in$ R , but (3, 2) $\notin R_{1}$

For $R_{2}$ : x + 2y = 10 and x, y $\in$ N

Possible values of x, and y are :

x = 8, y= 1    i.e    (8, 1)

x = 6, y = 2    i.e    (6, 2)

x = 4, y = 3    i.e    (4, 3) and

x = 2, y = 4    i.e    (2, 4)

$\therefore\,\,\, R_{2}$ = {(8, 1) (6, 2) (4, 3) (2, 4)}

$\therefore\,\,\,$ Range of $R_{2} = \left\{ {1,2,3,4} \right\} R_{2}$ is not symmetric and transitive

